{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-haikyu-the-volleyball-story-and-how-the-game-works/audio/main-fa3a458581f5.mp3","durationSec":220.704,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":0.62,"text":"Haikyu!!"},{"start":0.62,"end":2.74,"text":"is a Japanese manga about volleyball."},{"start":3.54,"end":6.2,"text":"A manga is a story told through words and pictures."},{"start":7.02,"end":8.88,"text":"Haruichi Furudate wrote and drew it."},{"start":9.38,"end":13.56,"text":"It appeared in the magazine Weekly Shonen Jump from 2012 to 2020."},{"start":14.2,"end":17.1,"text":"The complete manga has 45 volumes, or books."},{"start":17.1,"end":19.58,"text":"Production I.G made the TV anime."},{"start":20.3,"end":23.12,"text":"The anime brings the players, games, and sounds to the screen."},{"start":23.8,"end":28.58,"text":"By December 2025, the manga had over 75 million copies in circulation."},{"start":29.22,"end":32.92,"text":"Its story follows players who learn to use their different skills together."},{"start":33.84,"end":37.78,"text":"Shoyo Hinata is short, but he is very fast and can jump very high."},{"start":38.54,"end":44,"text":"While he is in junior high school, he sees Karasuno High School play volleyball on TV."},{"start":44.86,"end":46.66,"text":"One short player catches his attention."},{"start":47.38,"end":49.32,"text":"This player is called the Little Giant."},{"start":50.2,"end":51.28,"text":"Hinata feels inspired."},{"start":51.72,"end":52.84,"text":"He wants to play like him."},{"start":53.22,"end":56.8,"text":"However, Hinata’s own volleyball club has almost no members."},{"start":57.32,"end":59.88,"text":"His dream starts before he has a strong team."},{"start":60.58,"end":62.58,"text":"His height does not stop him from wanting to play."},{"start":63.28,"end":66.32,"text":"His speed and jump give him something important to build on."},{"start":67.2,"end":69.2,"text":"Tobio Kageyama is a genius setter."},{"start":69.92,"end":73.56,"text":"A setter sends the ball into a good place for another player to hit."},{"start":74.82,"end":76.96,"text":"Kageyama can do this very well."},{"start":77.7,"end":83.08,"text":"People call him the King of the Court because of his skill and his bossy way of treating others."},{"start":84.3,"end":87.94,"text":"Hinata’s team loses badly to Kageyama’s team in junior high school."},{"start":89.04,"end":92.34,"text":"Later, Hinata goes to Karasuno, hoping to beat him."},{"start":92.78,"end":95.24,"text":"But Kageyama joins Karasuno too."},{"start":96.18,"end":97.46,"text":"They are now on the same team."},{"start":100.11,"end":104.61,"text":"The rivals must learn to become partners, not just strong players on their own."},{"start":105.53,"end":108.31,"text":"Karasuno High School once had a strong volleyball team."},{"start":108.77,"end":111.79,"text":"The Little Giant played for Karasuno at the national tournament."},{"start":111.79,"end":114.69,"text":"Later, the team was no longer as strong."},{"start":115.39,"end":118.11,"text":"Other teams began calling it the Wingless Crows."},{"start":119.17,"end":121.63,"text":"The name suggests birds that cannot fly."},{"start":122.73,"end":127.19,"text":"Now Karasuno wants to return to the Nationals, a tournament with teams from across Japan."},{"start":128.15,"end":130.13,"text":"Hinata and Kageyama become part of this effort."},{"start":130.71,"end":132.87,"text":"The goal is bigger than their personal rivalry."},{"start":133.93,"end":137.69,"text":"Karasuno needs its players to work together so the team can become strong again."},{"start":138.77,"end":142.79,"text":"In indoor volleyball, each team has six players on the court."},{"start":142.79,"end":144.71,"text":"A net separates the teams."},{"start":144.71,"end":148.11,"text":"A rally starts with a serve from behind the end line."},{"start":148.69,"end":151.01,"text":"The teams then send the ball back and forth."},{"start":151.79,"end":154.95,"text":"A team has up to three touches before returning the ball."},{"start":155.67,"end":159.55,"text":"A common pattern is receive, set, and spike."},{"start":160.55,"end":164.39,"text":"Players receive the ball, set it up, then hit it over the net."},{"start":165.25,"end":167.79,"text":"Every rally gives one team a point."},{"start":168.41,"end":170.05,"text":"This is rally scoring."},{"start":170.05,"end":174.73,"text":"A team scores when the ball lands on the other side or the other team makes a mistake."},{"start":175.39,"end":179.75,"text":"Most sets go to 25 points, with a two-point lead needed to win."},{"start":179.75,"end":181.67,"text":"Players have different jobs."},{"start":182.25,"end":183.65,"text":"The setter sets up the ball."},{"start":184.23,"end":186.97,"text":"A wing spiker attacks from the sides near the net."},{"start":187.55,"end":191.27,"text":"A middle blocker plays near the centre of the net and blocks or attacks."},{"start":192.01,"end":195.85,"text":"A libero helps defend in the back row and wears a different-colour shirt."},{"start":196.27,"end":199.11,"text":"A block is a jump at the net to stop an attack."},{"start":199.95,"end":202.19,"text":"Hinata and Kageyama use a quick attack."},{"start":203.03,"end":206.71,"text":"Kageyama sends a low, fast set while Hinata is already jumping."},{"start":207.59,"end":210.21,"text":"Hinata’s speed and jump meet Kageyama’s skill."},{"start":210.95,"end":212.47,"text":"They need good timing and trust."},{"start":213.35,"end":214.23,"text":"This is why Haikyu!!"},{"start":214.23,"end":215.21,"text":"is about teamwork."},{"start":215.97,"end":220.21,"text":"One player’s strength becomes more useful when it connects with another player’s strength."}],"words":[{"text":"Haikyu","start":0,"end":0.62},{"text":"is","start":0.62,"end":1},{"text":"a","start":1,"end":1.14},{"text":"Japanese","start":1.14,"end":1.52},{"text":"manga","start":1.52,"end":1.86},{"text":"about","start":1.86,"end":2.2},{"text":"volleyball","start":2.2,"end